#### emits HTML layout Draw IR with computed style and hit geometry before raster

- Verify: emits HTML layout Draw IR with computed style and hit geometry before raster
   - Expected: batch.source.source_kind equals `html_ast`
   - Expected: card.component_id equals `card`
   - Expected: card.border_rect.present is true
   - Expected: card.content_rect.present is true
   - Expected: card.hit_rect.present is true
   - Expected: card.clip_rect.present is true
   - Expected: card.content_rect.x equals `card.x + 3`
   - Expected: card.content_rect.y equals `card.y + 3`
   - Expected: card.content_rect.width equals `40)  # oracle: 40 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: card.content_rect.height equals `18)  # oracle: 18 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: _draw_ir_style_value(card, "tag") equals `section`
   - Expected: _draw_ir_style_value(card, "display") equals `block`
   - Expected: _draw_ir_style_value(card, "padding-left") equals `2`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 21 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: emits HTML layout Draw IR with computed style and hit geometry before raster")
val html = "<html><head><style>#card { background-color:#1d4ed8; color:#ffffff; width:40px; height:18px; padding:2px; border:1px solid #0f172a; }</style></head><body><section id='card'>CMD</section></body></html>"
val composition = simple_web_layout_render_html_draw_ir(html, 96, 64)
val batch = composition.batches[0]
val card = _draw_ir_command_by_id(batch.commands, "card")

expect(batch.source.source_kind).to_equal("html_ast")
expect(batch.commands.len()).to_be_greater_than(0)
expect(card.component_id).to_equal("card")
expect(card.border_rect.present).to_equal(true)
expect(card.content_rect.present).to_equal(true)
expect(card.hit_rect.present).to_equal(true)
expect(card.clip_rect.present).to_equal(true)
expect(card.content_rect.x).to_equal(card.x + 3)
expect(card.content_rect.y).to_equal(card.y + 3)
expect(card.content_rect.width).to_equal(40)  # oracle: 40 — named expected value from the requirement
expect(card.content_rect.height).to_equal(18)  # oracle: 18 — named expected value from the requirement
expect(_draw_ir_style_value(card, "tag")).to_equal("section")
expect(_draw_ir_style_value(card, "display")).to_equal("block")
expect(_draw_ir_style_value(card, "padding-left")).to_equal("2")
```

</details>

